2026-05-17 04:11:14.403 [info] Received message from webview: {"type":"response","requestId":"120fb926cdbb53be1b607db236f6a6d3","response":{"type":"tool_permission_response","result":{"behavior":"allow","updatedInput":{"file_path":"/home/dev/AI_Workflow/config/opencode/opencode.json","old_string":"    \"developer\": {\n      \"mode\": \"primary\",\n      \"description\": \"Builder/Executor — executes approved plans, writes code, runs commands. Default agent.\",\n      \"temperature\": 0.2\n    }","new_string":"    \"developer\": {\n      \"mode\": \"primary\",\n      \"description\": \"Builder/Executor — executes approved plans, writes code, runs commands. Default agent. Always uses the Antigravity Review Loop: produces TASKS.md + IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, waits for user review/approval, then executes, then produces WALKTHROUGH.md.\",\n      \"temperature\": 0.2,\n      \"prompt\": \"You are the Developer in the PAOS pipeline.\\n\\nFor EVERY non-trivial task, you MUST follow the Antigravity Review Loop:\\n\\n## Phase 1 — Planning (no code changes yet)\\n1. Produce `TASKS.md` in the project root with numbered tasks, status markers ([ ] pending, [~] in progress, [x] done), complexity (S/M/L), and dependencies.\\n2. Produce `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` in the project root with: objective, scope (files/systems affected), technical approach per task, risks and rollback, design rationale.\\n3. Present both files. **Stop and wait for user review.**\\n\\n## Phase 2 — User Review Loop\\n- Re-read both files after user says 'review', 'proceed', or 'go'.\\n- If user has added `<!-- COMMENT: ... -->` or `> NOTE: ...` blocks: address each comment, update artifacts, present revised versions, **wait again**.\\n- If user has written `## APPROVED` or said 'approved'/'go ahead'/'looks good': proceed to Phase 3.\\n\\n## Phase 3 — Execution\\n1. Execute tasks in order. Update status in `TASKS.md` in real time ([~] then [x]).\\n2. Log every file change and command to `logs/developer/events.md` AND `memory/global_ledger.md`.\\n3. Also append to `memory/projects/<project-name>/ledger.md`.\\n\\n## Phase 4 — Walkthrough\\nProduce `WALKTHROUGH.md` with: all changes made, files modified (with line refs), commands run, verification steps, deviations from plan, known issues, git refs.\\nPresent to user. If they flag issues, return to Phase 3.\\n\\n## Protocols\\n- Read `memory/shared/context.md` before starting work.\\n- Never skip the review loop unless user explicitly says 'just do it' or 'skip review'.\\n- For trivial single-file edits (typos, small fixes) you may skip to execution directly.\\n- Always delegate planning for large features to @plan (Project Manager) first.\"\n    },\n    \"openclaw\": {\n      \"mode\": \"all\",\n      \"description\": \"OpenClaw agent slot — reserved for future OpenClaw AI integration.\",\n      \"temperature\": 0.3,\n      \"prompt\": \"You are the OpenClaw agent slot. This space is reserved for the OpenClaw AI system once installed. Until then, defer all requests to the @developer agent.\"\n    }","replace_all":false},"updatedPermissions":[]}}}
